  "beats": [
    {
      "t": "2026-11-20T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "According to Wikipedia, three Salvadoran soldiers were killed and another was injured on 20 November when explosives they were handling detonated.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1386870897:84"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-20T00:00:12Z",
      "text": "Since 21 October 2026, El Salvador has been conducting a military intervention in Haiti, after a gang ambush on 18 October led to four Salvadoran aviation technicians of the Gang Suppression Force being kidnapped.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1386870897:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-20T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "The map shows El Salvador, the country where the reports place this event.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-20:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-20T00:00:33Z",
      "text": "On 16 November, Salvadoran justice minister Gustavo Villatoro reiterated that all troops would withdraw once the technicians were recovered, and on 17 November demonstrators gathered in support.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:week:1386870897:54",
        "wiki:week:1386870897:123"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-20T00:00:42Z",
      "text": "On 18 November, Salvadoran helicopters destroyed a house in Canaan belonging to Jeff Larose, leader of the Taliban gang, but it is unknown whether Larose was killed.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:week:1386870897:75"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-20T00:00:51Z",
      "text": "On 20 November, Pélissier announced that it and El Salvador will build three new prisons to incarcerate gang members.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:week:1386870897:93"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-20T00:01:02Z",
      "text": "The article lists two sides: Gang Suppression Force, Task Force mercenaries and Logistical support on one, and Haitian gangs, 400 Mawozo and Chèn Méchan on the other.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1386870897:side-1",
        "wiki:box:1386870897:side-2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-20T00:01:09Z",
      "text": "Wikipedia lists the conflict as ongoing.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1386870897:status"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-20T00:01:16Z",
      "text": "According to Wikipedia, casualties on one side were 3 Salvadorans killed and 1 Salvadoran injured, and on the other side ~74 killed.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1386870897:casualties-side-1-",
        "wiki:box:1386870897:casualties-side-2-"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-20T00:01:25Z",
      "text": "The reports also name Ouest.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-20:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-20T00:01:34Z",
      "text": "La Prensa Gráfica and AP reported the story.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-20:5",
        "wiki:2026-11-20:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-20T00:01:42Z",
      "text": "Al Jazeera ran the headline “Haiti police say 34 gang members killed in capital raid.”",
      "cites": [
        "news:aljazeera:efddfae4739d"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-20T00:01:53Z",
      "text": "The sources are Wikipedia, its current events and articles, Wikimedia pageviews and Wikidata.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-20:5",
